# Poke 327

## Overview
This project is meant to be a Pokemon-like game. There is a 401x401 world map, which gets procedurally generated as the moves and maintains consistency with neighbouring maps. This update itroduces pathfinding logic using Dijikstra's algorithm needed for NPCs to caclulate travel costs to the Player Character.


## New Features: 1.04
    -  I have added NPC and PC movement. You cannot control the PC's movement yet, thats next, but right now it moves randomly and rival and hikers will chase after it using the distance maps from the last update. 
    -  I have also added wanderes('w'), explorers('e'), pacers('p') and sentrys('s'). The sentries don't move at all and the others move until reaching either the end of their terrain or to an impassable object, when it will move in the opposite direction.
    - I have also made the heap generic, so I could use it for the characters too.


## Running Instructions
1. Change directories(cd) into the below folder: 
Bash ```cd kochadampally_martin.assignment-1.05```

2. Clean the folder:
Bash ```make clean```

3. Compile the code:
Bash ```make poke327```

4. Run the code:
Bash ```./poke327```



## Previous Updates
### 1.03
    - Player Character Placement: The Player Character (@) is placed randomly somewhere along the road (#).
    - Dijikstra & Fibbonacci Heap Implementation: I have implemented a Fibonacci Heap to serve as the priority queue for my Dijikstra's Algorithim. I also to implemented a reference table to keep pointers to all elements currently in the heap, making deacrease_key easier.
    - Distance Maps: I run dijikstra's starting at the Player Charachter's position so that I can generate distance maps for each NPC to know the most efficient route the PC.
### 1.02
    I have implement the maps, so that they hold the position of the four gates and thier current x, y position in the world. I also added pointers from each of the squares to its surrounding squares, and updated this for the seeding code as well. Then moving on to the updates made for assignment-1.02, I used a queue to keep track of the maps created, so that i know what to free in the end, enqueuing maps as I create them. I then used a while loop, fgets and sscanf to get the get the commands from the user. I used the eq from the specs to reduce the number of buildings as you travel further away from rhe center, and assigned gates before world generation, to ensure consistency with neighbouring maps.

### 1.01
    The terrain is generated through through a seeding porocess. First we set all the characters on the map to null. Then I randomly select coordinates for each of the symbols representing different terrains and in the same order add them to the queue. Once the seeds have been sown, we call the seed_map function. This works by pulling each seed from the queue and replicate the seeds symbol to the surrounding squares, if that square is unassigned (Almost like a fungus). This functions iterates till there is no more space to grow.

    I added three more terrain elements than the ones specified by the specification and here they are:
        1. '^' which represents trees or a forest.
        2. '%' which represents a mountainous region.
        3. '*' which represents snow or the artic.

    Then we have road generation. This works by randomly generating the starting and ending positions of the road on the edge of the map and the point where they intersect. Then I just connect these point to form the road. I perform this twice: once for the vertical road and once for the horizontal road. After each generation, I pick a random point one the fist straight length of the road and place the pokemart and pokemon center. Lastly we generate the borders.
